prompts.match:
[REFERENCE FACTS]
{{REFERENCE_FACTS}}
[/REFERENCE FACTS]

[CANDIDATE UNITS]
{{CANDIDATE_UNITS}}
[/CANDIDATE UNITS]

For every reference fact, identify one candidate unit that states or entails its complete meaning. Similar topics and partial mentions are insufficient. Preserve actors, objects, quantities, negation, uncertainty, attribution, and event status. If several units qualify, choose the smallest unit ID. If no single unit qualifies, use null.

Return every reference fact exactly once and in order:
{"matches": [{"fact_idx": 0, "align_unit_idx": null}]}

prompts.decompose:
[SUMMARY]
{{SUMMARY}}
[/SUMMARY]

List all distinct factual claims made by this summary. This is decomposition, not selection: do not discard a claim because it is minor, implausible, or possibly false. Separate independently checkable claims and preserve attribution, quantities, negation, uncertainty, and event status. Do not use the original conversation or outside knowledge.

Return:
{"atomic_facts": ["<claim>", "<claim>"]}

prompts.verify:
[EVIDENCE]
{{EVIDENCE}}
[/EVIDENCE]

[CLAIMS]
{{CLAIMS}}
[/CLAIMS]

For every claim, decide whether the entire claim is justified by the evidence. Unsupported people, dates, numbers, certainty, attribution, causality, or event status make the claim not supported. Use no outside knowledge.

Return all claims in order:
{"verifications": [{"fact_idx": 0, "conclusion": "supported"}]}
The only allowed conclusions are "supported" and "not supported".
